# Managing Users in AD

## Lab Overview
This lab further directs users on how to manage OUs and User objects

## Objectives
- Learn how to delete and delegate users
- Ensure users have proper privilegs and access to resources
- Use Powershell to chanage user passwords

## Key Concepts
| Delegatation of Control Wizard | guided tool used for delegating specific administrative tasks(over an OU/container) |
| RDP | Microsoft protocol for remote login and control of Windows desktops
| Powershell | built-in Microsoft command-line shell and scripting language |

## Environment
Platform: TryHackMe
Operating System: Windows Server 2019
Directory Service: AD DS
Command-line Tool: Powershell

## Lab Walkthrough

### Delegate Control to a User over an OU(inside ADUC)
- Select 'View' from the top of the screen
- Select 'Advanced Features'
- Right-Click the OU that the user is delegating control over
- in the Delegation of Control Wizard, click 'Next'until you get to the Users and Groups section
- Click Add, type the name of the user/group that is being delegated control, then press 'Next'
- Check the box of the privilege that is to be delegated
- Click Finish to complete the process

### OU Deletion
- Right-Click on OU to be deleted
- Select Properties
- Select the Object Tab
- Uncheck the box that says "Protect object from accidental deletion"
- Select 'OK'
- Right-click the OU/User to be deleted
- Select 'Yes' when prompted to verify the deletion request

### Change Passwords(using Powershell)
- Run Powershell as Admin
- Type: Set-ADAccountPassword username123 -Reset -NewPassword (Read-Host -AsSecureString -Prompt 'New Password') -Verbose
- set new password(when prompted)

### Force a Password Resest(at next Logon)
- Run Powershell as Admin
- Type:  Set-ADuser -ChangePasswordAtLogon $true -Identity username123 -Verbose

