## Security Relevance
Large organizations may require users other than domain admins to handle administration of other users and groups. Delegating the correct amount of privilege needed for tasks increases efficiency and mitigates single points of failures and bottlenecks. Passwords are a common attack point for malicious actors, regularly changing passwords increases a organizations security profile.

## Key Takeaways
- Proper provisioning and configuration of accounts saves time and increases security
- RDP should be used along with a VPN to prevent direct exposure to the internet
- Powershell allows users who may not have access to Active Directory Software to still complete tasks

